Z||000000||William||10-24-2000||11:54 PM||||I'm I wrong or did I see a post in the past about a way of checking  the vin to see if a car had ever been in a wreck? I finally got around to adjusting the rear deck lid and I could not do it. it's level at the front in the rear it sits slightly higher on one side Now I'm concerned. The car had the original paint when I got it and all was equally faded so it would have been early on. I can't see any visable frame damage but what would I be looking for? I'm kinda getting mad thinking about this.||||reg||1
Z||000001||RobertVol||10-25-2000||12:10 AM||||William they still have that free car fax check I believe. Check it out http:/www.carfax.com<P>I am not saying that your has not been in a wreck but the panels on our beloved cars dont always line just perfect. Of course you should look for the normal things<P>1 - Underside piant overspray<BR>2 - If the car was damaged in rear end wreck<BR>    check for re - welding of the exaust   <BR>    on the underside.<BR>3 - Believe it or not also you can tell<BR>    because they dont use the same<BR>    replacment bolts when replacing body<BR>    parts. check and see if the bolts on<BR>    certain things such as rear deck are<BR>    different or the vent clamps are<BR>    different. This is not a tell tail sign<BR>    for this one but it may be.<P>Hope this helps <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT 55k  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||10-25-2000||11:58 AM||||The rubber bumpers at the corners of the trunk are adjustable for height. If one side was turn up for a few years it will warp the decklid. Just something else to look at.||||reg||1
Z||000003||jammer||10-27-2000||07:33 PM||||to check title history go to <A HREF="http://www.carfax.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carfax.com</A>    it was free for a while and may still be i checked one that was posted here and it showed a salvage title. i checked all of mine and found my 84 was in two wrecks not totoaled but it was noted.||||reg||1
Z||000004||William||10-27-2000||08:06 PM||||well I checked carfax but now you have to pay. I was suprised to find that they have 13 histories on this car,(Oh dear God), but they won't say what they are or if it's bad news. The next question is if I want to pay $15.00 to find out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||10-27-2000||08:23 PM||||When I had my 85 SE, I ran the carfax on it to see if it had the actual miles. The title history that I got was useless- it only went back a couple of years. They had a satisfaction guarantee, so I emailed them that I was not satisfied and they credited the charge back to my card with no questions asked. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||10-27-2000||11:22 PM||||I did the carfax report on mine. went back to 04/27/89 and showed only 3 tittle changes. <P>The van went back to 12/13/93 and showed 8 tittle changes. There's one recent after that in NY that doesn't show on the report.||||reg||1
